    "https://jobs.fu-berlin.de/job/Research-assistant-%28praedoc%29-%28fmd%29-%28DM-940%29/1450905333/": {
      "title": "Research assistant (praedoc) (f/m/d)",
      "description": "Research assistant (praedoc) (f/m/d) (DM-940) Job Details | Freie Universität Berlin We use cookies to offer you the best possible website experience. Your cookie preferences will be stored in your browser’s local storage. This includes cookies necessary for the website's operation. Additionally, you can freely decide and change any time whether you accept cookies or choose to opt out of cookies to improve website's performance, as well as cookies used to display content tailored to your interests. Your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer may be impacted if you do not accept all cookies. Modify Cookie Preferences Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies Skip to main content Home Other Job Offers Accessibility Accessibility Easy Read Contact FAQ Search by Keyword Home Other Job Offers Accessibility Accessibility Easy Read Contact FAQ Language Deutsch (Deutschland) English (United States) View Profile Search by Keyword Show More Options Loading... Personnel category All Division/Department All Length of employment All Salary/pay grade All Full-time/part-time All Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Research assistant (praedoc) (f/m/d) (DM-940) Department: Department of Biology, Chemistry, Pharmacy contract duration: limited to 4 years Salary / pay grade: E 13 TV-L FU Working hours: 67 % Requisition ID: 940 Application deadline: 23.11.2026 Salary calculator TV-L Salary Student assistant TV Stud III Who We Are The Heinke group explores novel functional materials, like thin films of nanoporous metal-organic frameworks (MOFs), and their physicochemical properties. By state-of-the-art spectroscopy techniques, the understanding of the interactions at the molecular level is enhanced. The focus is on the diffusion and adsorption of guest molecules in the pores, ion conduction and (opto)electronic properties of these modern functional films as well as their applications, e.g. for molecular separation and as unique sensors. \"Smart\" materials with remote-controllable properties, especially by means of light, are also being prepared and explored. https://www.bcp.fu-berlin.de/chemie/chemie/forschung/PhysTheoChem/agheinke/index.html What You Can Expect in Your New Role Nanoporous thin films of metal-organic frameworks (MOFs) will be prepared and investigated. The focus is on the physicochemical properties of the thin films and the interaction with the guest molecules in the pores. The focus is on per- and polyfluorinated alkyl compounds (PFAS). In particular, the uptake and mass transport in the pores, i.e. diffusion, will be investigated using various techniques, such as quartz crystal microbalance, infrared and Raman spectroscopy. The work of this PhD project will be carried out within the framework of the CRC-1349 \"Fluorine-Specific Interactions\". The call and hiring are subject to the approval of the third funding period from 2027-2030 by the DFG at the end of November 2026. Key Requirements Completed university degree (Master/Diploma) in chemistry, physics, materials science, chemical engineering, or a related subject Desirable Experience in one (or more) of the following areas would be beneficial: metal-organic frameworks; adsorption and diffusion; Infrared and Raman spectroscopy and/or quartz crystal microbalance A strong motivation for research and good experimental skills Excellent written and oral English skills. In addition, German language skills would be an advantage, but are not required. Organizational skills You should have the ability to work both independently and in a team. Benefits and Other Advantages Modern workplace in the leafy suburb of Dahlem Job security Salary in line with the collective agreement for the civil service at the state level (TV-L FU), plus additional one-off annual payment Flexible working hours and mobile working by arrangement, where possible The compatibility of work and family life Thirty days of vacation (based on a five-day working week) Office closed on December 24 and December 31 Numerous training and continuing education options for professional and personal development Opportunity to participate in University Sports Center courses and the health promotion program Free parking close to the office and good public transportation connections Discounted “Job Ticket” for public transportation Free use of the Freie Universität library system Employee discount in the cafeteria Exclusive deals for products and services through Corporate Benefits If you are interested in what we have to offer, then you can send your application materials to us directly. Simply submit your application exclusively via our career portal by clicking the “Apply now” button. Unfortunately, we cannot consider applications by post or by e-mail. You can also get in touch with Mr. Prof. Dr. Lars Heinke ( lars.heinke@fu-berlin.de ). Please note Freie Universität Berlin is an equal opportunity employer. Apply now » Find similar jobs: Service Navigation Home Contact Legal Notice Data Protection Information Accessibility Easy Read FAQ Social Media Instagram Youtube Facebook LinkedIn Mastodon Bluesky Information about Using Social Media × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the website to function: \"route\" is used for session stickiness \"careerSiteCompanyId\" is used to send the request to the correct data center \"JSESSIONID\" is placed on the visitor's device during the session so the server can identify the visitor \"Load balancer cookie\" (actual cookie name may vary)  prevents a visitor from bouncing from one instance to another Cookies from provider SAPasserviceprovider are required and cannot be turned off Confirm My Choices Reject All Cookies Accept All Cookies"
    },
